{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>And he gathered all the food</b> — this refers to Joseph mentioned above, and also afterward, \"and Joseph laid up grain\" (Genesis 41:48), and likewise \"for it was beyond number\" (Genesis 41:49) — Joseph is the one mentioned. Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 41:48) said that the meaning is not \"all,\" for people were dying of famine, and likewise \"and all the earth came to Egypt\" (Genesis 41:57) — rather, the reason is that he gathered all that he could. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that he gathered everything under his authority, and he distributed to them from it each year enough for their sustenance, so that they would not waste it. This is what is said: \"And let them gather all the food of the good years, and let them lay up grain under the hand of Pharaoh, food in the cities, and let them keep it\" (Genesis 41:35). And because it says \"and let them gather all the food\" and it says \"and let them lay up grain,\" and likewise \"and he gathered all the food\" / \"and Joseph laid up grain,\" this indicates that they gathered everything edible to man — grain and bread and food, even figs and raisins and the like — and they laid up from them the grain under the hand of Pharaoh, that being the produce that was brought in with the winnowing fork and the sieve to winnow and to clean, and he placed it in cities for eating of all the fruits. And all the food was kept in storage for the need of the years of famine, so that they would take from it enough for their livelihood, while what remained of the grain was maintained in the storehouses. And it is possible that he gave them money at a cheap price from the king's treasuries, and therefore the grain belonged to Pharaoh, and he sold it to them in the years of famine, as it is written (Genesis 47:14), \"And Joseph gathered up all the money that was found in the land of Egypt\" — or that the king acquired it by force, for he said, I have kept it. But Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 41:48) translated אֹכֶל and בָּר identically."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:54.379502490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}